MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The retaining-washer and self-drilling screw assortments fit my ongoing repair and fabrication interests: they complement the cotter pins, rivets, drill bits, and fastening kits I have used.",
    "The hook-and-loop tape and duct tape suit practical mounting and securing jobs. Removable mounting and temporary repairs give them useful roles alongside my existing double-sided adhesive tape."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The compressor filter and fuel flow meter require particular equipment and tasks that my history does not establish. Buying workshop tools does not mean I have a compressed-air setup or need to measure fuel transfers.",
    "The mushroom-cultivation filters and door hanger miss my current repair and fabrication purpose. Their adhesive or hanging functions alone do not make them useful for the work I am considering."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in tools seems to have been stretched into an interest in specialized equipment without evidence that I have a use for it.",
    "Shared words or functions such as adhesive, mounting, and hardware seem to count too much when the actual application differs from my projects."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of fastener assortments suggest that having several sizes available for repairs matters to me; a single screw size is less compelling without a specific need.",
    "General relevance is different from something I would choose now. The wood screws and M2.5 standoffs interest me, but their exact dimensions need to match an upcoming project before I would buy them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair and fastening interests but sometimes assumed equipment ownership or a specific project need that my history does not establish."
}
